  "Solution": {
    "S": "Cost = $x^2 + 78x + 2500$.\n\nPrice per unit $p = 600 - 8x$.\n\nSelling price = $x(600 - 8x) = 600x - 8x^2$.\n\nProfit $P(x) = (600x - 8x^2) - (x^2 + 78x + 2500) = -9x^2 + 522x - 2500$.\n\n$P'(x) = -18x + 522 = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 29$.\n\n$P''(x) = -18 < 0$, so maximum at $x = 29$.\n\n$P(29) = -9(29)^2 + 522(29) - 2500 = -9(841) + 15138 - 2500 = -7569 + 15138 - 2500 = 5069$.\n\nThus the correct option is A: ₹ 5069."
  },
